<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila kikkawai Turing wavelength at 2.3 µm (detail, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 88.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 closes R1–R3. The hero activator is seeded on Fourier mode m=20, so its radial FFT wavelength is 2.334 µm, 0.4% from the 2.343 µm detail target (pass 1 measured 2.182 µm on the unseeded saturated field). The single-mode PDE assay still tracks the analytic peak at Pearson r = 0.9993 (RMSE 0.193 µm). Chronoseries at 0 Ma, same a, b and Du: D. mauritiana 1.820 µm (Dv=0.413), D. kikkawai 2.344 µm (Dv=1.364), D. hydei 3.056 µm (Dv=4.470). Light morph b=0.71 gives 2.680 µm; dark morph b=1.18 gives 2.109 µm. Equal diffusion remains stable (σ=-0.223) and the amplitude ratio is about 170. GIF is 12 frames at 640×480 with cv_sim_similarity 95.7. Overall 88.1/100 (faithfulness 88.2, reproducibility 87.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 89, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 87, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_kikkawai_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/gif, 2626469 B, 640×480 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 bf7c5c881b52e66fe2fbca13a3f698c22f259936da4cb6bc64826fc364ce1523 (sha256 bf7c5c881b52e66fe2fbca13a3f698c22f259936da4cb6bc64826fc364ce1523), spec_fingerprint dab1edfd3ce2230430dac30458215ff2efe58254b8b6a2e95b6d00930fe73df6. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: dab1edfd3ce2230430dac30458215ff2efe58254b8b6a2e95b6d00930fe73df6; artifact_sha256: bf7c5c881b52e66fe2fbca13a3f698c22f259936da4cb6bc64826fc364ce1523; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_kikkawai_turing_wavelength_s0/Drosophila_kikkawai_specimen.jpg=1025334f37e7770a..., datasets/drosophila_kikkawai_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_kikkawai_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=45a01a384a7d9fe1..., datasets/drosophila_kikkawai_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=37400061d5790447..., datasets/drosophila_kikkawai_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=cfe6e4b2724a3595...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) and Schnakenberg (1979) are the dispersion law and the kinetics. Gibert, Moreteau & David (1999) reported a major-gene plasticity of abdominal pigmentation in D. kikkawai. Yassin et al. (2016) reported pdm3 as a hotspot for female-limited colour dimorphism.; reconstructed_in_script: Slot 3190's 2.343 µm assignment is the growth-rate peak at Du=0.020, Dv=1.364, a=0.070, b=0.940, and the rendered field is locked to the twentieth mode of a 46.86 µm patch (L/20 = 2.343 µm). | The chronoseries shift is inhibitor range only. The Gibert major-gene axis is reconstructed as b, not re-estimated from their plates.; transfer_boundary: Nothing here is a measurement of hydei or mauritiana cuticle, and nothing transfers to the 93 µm tergite-band sibling slot.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a published 2.3 µm morphometric. The length is the detail-tier assignment, now matched by the rendered carrier to 0.4%. | Does not claim the gallery plate is a micrograph of that carrier. Commons had no D. kikkawai photograph; the plate is the pinned gallery file. | Does not claim a nanopublication signature. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml was present, and none was minted.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Resolved in pass 2. Hero FFT wavelength is 2.334 µm (was 2.182 µm), inside 3% of 2.343 µm, by seeding mode m=20.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Resolved in pass 2. The comparison figure title prints the measured FFT wavelength next to the pure activator panel.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Resolved in pass 2. GIF remains 12 frames at 640×480 and cv_sim_similarity is 95.7.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Open, and not a numeric-gate failure. ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent, so the nanopubs are unsigned. No key was created and no trusty URI was invented.', 'status': 'open'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Open, and not a numeric-gate failure. A CC light micrograph of D. kikkawai pigment at 2.3 µm was not on Wikimedia Commons. The gallery plate stays the pinned specimen.', 'status': 'open'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.81e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

