<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila kikkawai Turing wavelength at 2.3 µm (detail, 0 Ma) (Drosophila kikkawai)",
        "Drosophila kikkawai Turing wavelength at 2.3 µm (detail, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Drosophila kikkawai morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila kikkawai specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila kikkawai" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a nanopublication signature. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml was present, and none was minted.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim a published 2.3 µm morphometric. The length is the detail-tier assignment, now matched by the rendered carrier to 0.4%.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the gallery plate is a micrograph of that carrier. Commons had no D. kikkawai photograph; the plate is the pinned gallery file.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Slot 3190's 2.343 µm assignment is the growth-rate peak at Du=0.020, Dv=1.364, a=0.070, b=0.940, and the rendered field is locked to the twentieth mode of a 46.86 µm patch (L/20 = 2.343 µm).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The chronoseries shift is inhibitor range only. The Gibert major-gene axis is reconstructed as b, not re-estimated from their plates.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) and Schnakenberg (1979) are the dispersion law and the kinetics. Gibert, Moreteau & David (1999) reported a major-gene plasticity of abdominal pigmentation in D. kikkawai. Yassin et al. (2016) reported pdm3 as a hotspot for female-limited colour dimorphism.",
        "transfer_boundary: Nothing here is a measurement of hydei or mauritiana cuticle, and nothing transfers to the 93 µm tergite-band sibling slot." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila kikkawai (Circumtropical Montium Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_kikkawai_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Drosophila kikkawai; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) and Schnakenberg (1979) are the dispersion law and the kinetics. Gibert, Moreteau & David (1999) reported a major-gene plasticity of abdominal pigmentation in D. kikkawai. Yassin et al. (2016) reported pdm3 as a hotspot for female-limited colour dimorphism.; reconstructed_in_script: Slot 3190's 2.343 µm assignment is the growth-rate peak at Du=0.020, Dv=1.364, a=0.070, b=0.940, and the rendered field is locked to the twentieth mode of a 46.86 µm patch (L/20 = 2.343 µm). | The chronoseries shift is inhibitor range only. The Gibert major-gene axis is reconstructed as b, not re-estimated from their plates.; transfer_boundary: Nothing here is a measurement of hydei or mauritiana cuticle, and nothing transfers to the 93 µm tergite-band sibling slot.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a published 2.3 µm morphometric. The length is the detail-tier assignment, now matched by the rendered carrier to 0.4%. | Does not claim the gallery plate is a micrograph of that carrier. Commons had no D. kikkawai photograph; the plate is the pinned gallery file. | Does not claim a nanopublication signature. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml was present, and none was minted.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2016.07.016>,
